Let the function $f(x)=-2m+2m\sin \left(x+ \dfrac {3\pi}{2}\right)-2\cos ^{2}\left(x- \dfrac {\pi}{2}\right)+1$, where $x\in\left[- \dfrac {\pi}{2},0\right]$, have a minimum value of $h(m)$.  
$(1)$ Find $h(m)$;  
$(2)$ If $h(m)= \dfrac {1}{2}$, find $m$ and the maximum value of $f(x)$ at this time.

