$(1)$ Find $h(m)$;  
$(2)$ If $h(m)= \dfrac {1}{2}$, find $m$ and the maximum value of $f(x)$ at this time.

Given a circle C: $x^2+y^2+x-6y+m=0$ and a line $l: x+2y-3=0$.

(1) When $m= \frac {5}{4}$, determine the positional relationship between circle C and line $l$;  
(2) If line $l$ and circle C have no common points, find the range of values for $m$;  
(3) If line $l$ intersects circle C at points P and Q, and O is the origin, and the circle with diameter PQ passes through point O, find the value of the real number $m$.

